# TradeBot project rules

## Source of truth

Before changing code, read `HANDSOFF.md`, `README.md`, and `RUN.md` when run steps matter. Align with `.cursor/agents/tradebot-editor.md`.

## Web file size (developer-owned)

Target **≤300 lines** per file under:

- `web/src/app/**`
- `web/src/components/**` except `ui/` (shadcn)
- `web/src/hooks/**`
- `web/src/lib/**`

**Excluded:** `web/src/components/ui/**`, generated files (`next-env.d.ts`, auto-managed Next blocks in `AGENTS.md`).

If a file is at or over the limit, split by responsibility (feature subfolder, hook, `lib/` helper) before adding large blocks.

No pass-through re-export files at `components/` root — import from the feature folder (see `web-components.mdc`).

## Living rules

When a new convention is agreed (architecture, naming, limits), add or update a focused `.mdc` in `.cursor/rules/` in the same session. One concern per file; clear `description` in frontmatter.

## Python

No line-count rule unless a separate `.mdc` is added later.
